{"reason": "The baseline validation accuracy peaks early at 0.8194 before suffering from loss divergence and overfitting, caused by asymmetric continuous-only Mixup corrupting feature-label alignment, overparameterized full-rank cross layers, and continuous scaling of discrete binary indicators. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation resolves these bottlenecks simultaneously across data representation, network capacity, and optimization. Reclassifying binary flags into categorical embeddings alongside group aggregations provides cleaner tabular signals, low-rank cross layers with continuous skip connections regularize interaction complexity, and tabular swap-noise with warm-up optimization prevents memorization without corrupting categorical semantics.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Reassign binary flags (CryoSleep, VIP, ZeroSpend, IsAlone) and a composite CabinDeck_CabinSide interaction to categorical embeddings, while engineering group-level manifest aggregations including group CryoSleep rate and group TotalSpend. WHY: Scaling discrete binary indicators with continuous scalers distorts their discrete nature, while companions traveling in groups exhibit strong spatial and social co-dependence that group aggregations effectively expose. HOW: Move CryoSleep, VIP, ZeroSpend, IsAlone, and the concatenated CabinDeck_CabinSide into categorical_cols for OrdinalEncoder, calculate non-leaking group-level aggregations mapped from group statistics, and apply RobustScaler strictly to true continuous numerical columns on the training fold. Interface constraints: Retain existing variable names categorical_cols, numerical_cols, train_split, val_split, test_features, cat_cardinalities, and preserve tensor output shapes.", "model_design": "WHAT: Refactor CrossLayer to utilize a low-rank matrix decomposition wi